<article class="env-definition" id="05RZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05RZ">Definition <span data-tag="05RZ">13.13.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $\alpha : K^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ be a morphism of $K(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A}))$. We say that $\alpha $ is a <em>filtered quasi-isomorphism</em> if the morphism $\text{gr}(\alpha )$ is a quasi-isomorphism. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $K^\bullet $ be an object of $K(\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A}))$. We say that $K^\bullet $ is <em>filtered acyclic</em> if the complex $\text{gr}(K^\bullet )$ is acyclic. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>